+# Expose initial image preparation during model pulls
+
+`models pull` performs its volume-space preflight through the selected inspector
+image. When that image is absent, Docker downloads and extracts it inside a
+captured JSON-report subprocess, hiding progress until completion. The pinned
+vLLM 0.28.0 image took roughly fifteen minutes on 2026-09-09; Docker remained
+responsive and the image and exact model snapshot eventually verified.
+
+Add explicit stage reporting and bounded progress for image resolution before
+the JSON cache probe, preserving confirmation, pinning, one downloader, and
+snapshot verification. A quiet subprocess is not evidence of a stalled daemon;
+do not start a competing cache writer or force-restart Docker to obtain status.
+
+Evidence: the dated Qwen3.8 concurrency trial's friction log and private native
+pull transcript. This does not invalidate its later measured capacity cells.
